  "notes": [
    "DEMO DATA standing in for the daily_totals table. Nothing outside lib/demo may import this file.",
    "Covers the 29 days BEFORE the demo day. Today's row is not stored here — lib/demo computes it from day.json and foods.json and appends it, so the dashboard and the trend charts can never disagree.",
    "Composed to exercise all three storage-class alert windows at once: vitamin C (storage 'none', 3-day window) dips below 70% of the RDA for the last three days and fires; magnesium (storage 'moderate', 7-day window) stays adequate throughout and does not fire; vitamin D (storage 'high', 30-day window) never looks alarming on any single day but averages around half the RDA across the month, which is exactly the pattern a daily alert would miss.",
    "coverage is the fraction of that day's entries that had any phytonutrient data. It hovers around a third, which is realistic — USDA's flavonoid databases cover ~500 foods against FoodData Central's 600,000.",
    "weights are deliberately noisy. Day-to-day bodyweight swings by a kilo or more on water alone, so a weight card that reacts to a single reading is reading noise. The trend line is the signal, and the UI says so."
  ],

